---
import fs from 'node:fs';
import path from 'node:path';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Film from '../components/Film.astro';

// Only this folder. public/media itself holds work footage, which does not belong here.
const dir = path.join(process.cwd(), 'public', 'media', 'personal');
const files = fs.existsSync(dir) ? fs.readdirSync(dir) : [];
const label = (f) => f.replace(/\.[^.]+$/, '').replace(/[-_]/g, ' ');
const videos = files.filter((f) => /\.(mp4|webm)$/i.test(f)).sort();
const stems = new Set(videos.map((f) => f.replace(/\.[^.]+$/, '')));
// An image sharing a video's name is that video's poster, not a photograph.
const photos = files
  .filter((f) => /\.(jpe?g|png|webp|avif)$/i.test(f))
  .filter((f) => !stems.has(f.replace(/\.[^.]+$/, '')))
  .sort();
const posterFor = (v) => {
  const stem = v.replace(/\.[^.]+$/, '');
  const hit = files.find((f) => f !== v && f.startsWith(stem + '.') && /\.(jpe?g|png|webp)$/i.test(f));
  return hit ? `/media/personal/${hit}` : undefined;
};
const hasMedia = photos.length > 0 || videos.length > 0;
---
<Base title="Off the clock · Amartya Gaur" description="The parts of Amartya Gaur that are not infrastructure: music, martial arts, and talking to rooms full of people about WordPress." theme="light">
  <article class="light sec about">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h1 class="d d-2">The rest of it</h1>
      <p class="lede">Everywhere else on this site I am an engineer. Here I am a person who owns
        several instruments and is competent on some of them.</p>

      <div class="cols">
        <section>
          <h2 class="mono sub">Music</h2>
          <p>I sing, and I play harmonium, tabla and guitar. The harmonium and the tabla came first and are the ones
            I would put money on; the guitar is the one I actually pick up, which tells you something about how
            practice works.</p>
          <p>There is a straight line between this and the day job, and I only noticed it recently. Tabla is a
            grammar: a fixed vocabulary of strokes, composed into cycles, where the interesting part is the return
            to the first beat rather than anything clever in the middle. I have spent five years building systems
            that behave the same way and calling it architecture.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="mono sub">Rooms full of people</h2>
          <p>Four WordCamps, in Mumbai, Ahmedabad, Delhi and Kolkata, mostly the same talk about building Gutenberg
            blocks, given three times, improving slightly each time. Speaking is the fastest way I know to find out
            whether you actually understand something. An audience finds the hole in your explanation in about
            forty seconds.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="mono sub">Elsewhere</h2>
          <p>I built the site for the Jeet Kune Do Federation of India for nothing, which is the sort of thing you
            do when the cause is close to you.</p>
          <p>I make AI video, which is how <a href="https://github.com/calesthio/OpenMontage/pull/372" rel="noopener">product-motion</a>
            happened. I wanted a tool that could cut a product film from the product&rsquo;s own source code, without
            inventing screens that do not exist, and it was easier to build it than to keep being disappointed.</p>
          <p>Bengaluru, mostly. An Arctic Code Vault contributor, which means only that I was committing to the
            right repositories in 2020.</p>
        </section>
      </div>

      {hasMedia ? (
        <div class="gallery">
          {videos.map((f) => (
            <div class="shot wide">
              <Film src={`/media/personal/${f}`} poster={posterFor(f)} caption={label(f)} />
            </div>
          ))}
          {photos.map((f) => (
            <figure class="shot">
              <img src={`/media/personal/${f}`} alt={label(f)} loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
              <figcaption class="mono">{label(f)}</figcaption>
            </figure>
          ))}
        </div>
      ) : (
        <p class="empty mono">Pictures of any of this to follow, once I find some that I like.</p>
      )}

      <p class="back mono"><a href="/">← back to the infrastructure</a></p>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .about { padding-top: clamp(120px, 14vw, 190px); }
  .about .lede { max-width: 42ch; }
  .cols { display: grid; gap: clamp(34px, 4vw, 56px); margin-top: clamp(48px, 6vw, 80px); border-top: 1px solid var(--rule); padding-top: 36px; }
  @media (min-width: 900px) { .cols { grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); } }
  .sub { color: var(--fail-ink); margin-bottom: 16px; }
  .cols p { color: var(--ink-2); font-size: var(--t-body); }
  .cols p + p { margin-top: 1em; }
  .cols a { color: var(--fail-ink); }

  .gallery { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(240px, 1fr)); gap: 20px; margin-top: clamp(44px, 5vw, 72px); }
  .shot { margin: 0; }
  .shot.wide { grid-column: span 2; }
  @media (max-width: 620px) { .shot.wide { grid-column: span 1; } }
  .shot img, .shot video { width: 100%; height: auto; display: block; background: var(--paper-2); border: 1px solid var(--rule); }
  .shot figcaption { margin-top: 9px; color: var(--mid); }
  .empty { margin-top: clamp(44px, 5vw, 68px); color: var(--mid); border-top: 1px solid var(--rule); padding-top: 26px; }
  .back { margin-top: clamp(50px, 6vw, 80px); color: var(--mid); }
  .back a { text-decoration: none; }
  .back a:hover { color: var(--ink); }
</style>
